{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-tm-heavy-atom-examples-table1-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:tm-heavy-atom-examples-table1-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table 1 from tm-heavy-atom-examples","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tm-heavy-atom-examples"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"tm-heavy-atom-examples-table1-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:tm-heavy-atom-examples-table1-data\"></a><p>For a nucleon count <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code>, the quantities below locate <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> relative to\nthe magic numbers <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{0, 2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126\\}</code> and fix the\nouter-shell occupancy that the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Q</code>-value algorithm consumes. For\nexample, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X = 33</code> sits just past the closure at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">28</code>, so\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m_{\\leq}(33) = 28</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_{\\mathrm{out}}(33) = 5</code>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Quantity</th>\n<th>Definition</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m_{\\leq}(X)</code></td>\n<td>Largest magic number <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\leq X</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_{\\mathrm{out}}(X)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X - m_{\\leq}(X)</code> (outer shell occupancy; <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">= 0</code> if magic)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_{\\mathrm{shell}}(X)</code></td>\n<td>Size of the shell containing <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-transfer-matrices/tm-heavy-atom-examples-table1-data.md","heading":"Table"}
